  "claim_boundary": "This v1 publisher scaffold is production-disabled. It can create and fully revalidate only explicitly synthetic qualification-chain artifacts, which are always marked synthetic_test_backend_not_evidence, real_host_observation=false, eligible_as_host_qualification_input=false, and validated_eligible_as_host_qualification_input=false. Synthetic source receipts retain their qualification-owned projection v2 and are never accepted as production input. A pure raw-Audit adapter core now performs single-descriptor artifact reading, strict Audit v2 versus failure-v1 separation, caller capture-envelope binding, source-pin checks, content-ID basis reconstruction, and independent observed-to-conformance recomputation; it emits only windows-event-log-source-audit-artifact-adapter-snapshot.v1 with projection_emitted=false, real_provisioner_observation=false, and every authorization false. The caller capture envelope is explicitly non-authoritative, hashes are not identity signatures, no production PowerShell acquisition or independent live control-plane reobservation exists, and the adapter cannot prove a real process origin, refresh, continuous stability, trusted execution, boot identity observation, replay exclusion, or tamper resistance. Raw Audit v2 makes nonconformance exit 2, requires explicit AllowSourceCreation intent for an absent-source Provision, exposes nontransactional partial failure and refresh uncertainty, and compares both endpoints; none of those same-process observations proves source history. The protocol separates human declarations from machine observations: hashes content-address the declaration but do not authenticate the operator, prove Intel Defaults, prove a cold boot, prove tuning is absent, or prove that the old host-block receipt came from the same physical chassis. A future production revision must freeze and audit a real fixed probe, direct PowerShell capture, failure-v1 quarantine, independent post-refresh source reobservation, process containment, same-machine/same-boot Application and System cursor continuity, cooldown and terminal-tail fault coverage, raw Event XML classification, and a separately reviewed outer consumer bridge with a new production projection schema and predicate. The current outer protocol exact-schema rejects terminal v2 and remains production-disabled. Even a future fully validated eligible host qualification would only support a bounded local host observation; it would not authorize CUDA by itself and would not prove general host stability, long-context information utilization, independent subjects, long companionship, multiple sessions, production ACTIVE, Appendable, Readable, Learnable, Steerable, or the four-capability system claim."
